## Field contract

Preserve:

```js
{
  parameter,
  value,
  onChange,
  error,
  disabled,
  parameterContext,
}
```

`value` is the complete current value of this parameter.

Treat object/array values as immutable.

`onChange(nextValue)` replaces the complete value.

Display `error` when appropriate.

When `disabled` is true, prevent every change.

Use `parameterContext` instead of refetching data already supplied by the host.

## ReadOnly contract

Preserve:

```js
{
  parameter,
  value,
  parameterContext,
}
```

Present the same canonical value without mutation.

## `parameterContext`

Frontend receives:

```js
{
  model,
  alternatives,
  criteriaTree,
  leafCriteria,
}
```

Backend receives a different `context`.

Do not rename or unify them.

## Frontend/Backend agreement

The Field, ReadOnly component and Backend validator must share one canonical value contract.

Inspect the generated Backend package when necessary.

Do not invent a separate Frontend-only value shape without an explicitly required normalization boundary.

## Expression Domains

Do not treat every parameter as an Expression Domain evaluation.

If and only if this parameter stores a criterion-domain evaluation, reuse the public Expression Domain input/validation infrastructure using the canonical domain from `parameterContext`.

Do not recreate registered numeric, linguistic, fuzzy or 2-tuple controls/validation.

